    "## Detailed Progress Report\n",
    "### 1. Initial Literature Review\n",
    "**Objective:** To establish a robust methodology to identify abandoned agricultural lands.\n",
    "**Action Items:**\n",
    "1. Read relavent literatures\n",
    "**Status:** ✅ Completed  \n",
    "**Notes:** Using @yinMappingAgriculturalLand2018 (For OBIA), @daraMappingTimingCropland2018 (For Classification), @alcantaraMappingExtentAbandoned2013 (For sample generation strategy) \n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Training Sample Generation for Agriculture Land Probability Classification\n",
    "1. Create a binary mask of all the agricultural lands from 2000-2022 (note that the land cover dataset for 2012 is not available).  \n",
    "    **Status:** ✅ Completed  \n",
    "    **Notes:** Used FRTC land cover dataset for identifying stable agriculture lands.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Identify the stable agricultural areas by finding the intersection of all the binary masks.\n",
    "    **Status:** ✅ Completed  \n",
    "    **Notes:** Intersected the annual agricultural masks to isolate pixels consistently classified as agriculture across all available years (2000-2022).\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Remove the small pixel clusters, field boundaries using the morphological operations.  \n",
    "    **Status:** ✅ Completed  \n",
    "    **Notes:** Applied a 2-pixel erosion to eliminate boundary/edge effects, and filtered out isolated pixel clusters smaller than 10 pixels (~0.9 ha) to guarantee sample purity.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. Convert the final stable agricultural land pixels to points  \n",
    "    **Status:** ✅ Completed  \n",
    "    **Notes:** Extracted an initial pool of 100,000 random sample points from within the pure, stable agricultural mask.\n",
    "\n",
    "5. Spatial thinning of the points  \n",
    "    **Status:** ✅ Completed  \n",
    "    **Notes:** Applied a spatial filter enforcing a 2,000-meter minimum distance between points to mitigate spatial autocorrelation and ensure broad geographic representation.\n",
    "\n",
    "6. Final check using a phenology profile of the points to ensure they strictly exhibit agricultural characteristics (sharp increase and decrease in NDVI).  \n",
    "    **Status:** ⚙️ In Progress | Estimated Completion: 02-04-2026 (2-3 Days)  \n",
    "    **Notes:** Performing multi-temporal phenological filtering on training samples to ensure they consistently exhibit active agricultural signatures (e.g., high NDVI amplitude indicating plow/harvest cycles)\n",
    "\n",
    "7. Repeat the same for the stable non-agricultural lands.  \n",
    "    **Status:** ⬜ Not Started    \n",
    "    **Notes:** Will perform stratified sampling using the 2022 land cover dataset to ensure the model learns the spectral signatures of all non-cropland classes. Dominant land covers (forest, rangeland, bare soil/sand, water, and built-up areas) will be proportionally represented to minimize confusion errors.\n",
